  "name": "Seudati (Acehnese body-percussion dance-song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Acehnese dance-song, strongest in Pidie and along the north coast, performed by eight male dancers led by a syeh, with two singers (aneuk syahi) who sing the verses. No instruments are used: the rhythm comes from finger snaps, slaps to the chest and sides (the hand-clap card stands in) and stamping, and the verses range over religious, historical and topical themes.",
